IMPORT prelude

-- State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL), not the daydate library. The
-- Act counts its periods in days "after the day on which" something happens (ss 21(3), (4), 76, 78, 105(5), (6)): the
-- day of the event is excluded, so the last day of a period of N days is the day N days after it (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 2026-09-07: "State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004", State
-- of Western Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- "within the period of N days after the day on which ...": the last day of the period.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is after` `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`
